    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 30 Elm Park is a stylish three/four-bedroom family home ideally located just off the Gort Road in Ennis. Built in 1983 and modernised and extended by the current Vendors in recent years, the property is within walking distance of the new Ennis Swimming & Leisure Centre and convenient to schools, shops, Ennis town centre and a host of local amenities.\n\nThe property offers well-proportioned family accommodation with a high standard of fixtures and fittings throughout. The ground floor comprises a spacious open-plan kitchen/living/dining room, with the rear extension featuring three skylights, double doors and a rear-aspect window, creating a bright and welcoming space with direct access to the garden. A utility room and bathroom are located off the kitchen, with access from the utility room to the side pergola. A ground-floor bedroom with open fireplace and front-aspect window completes this level.\nUpstairs are two large double bedrooms, a single bedroom and the main bathroom.\n\nThe property enjoys generous gardens, excellent off-street parking and an enclosed garage to the side, accessed via double timber doors. The front garden comprises a concrete driveway, lawn area and three planting boxes. The enclosed rear garden is predominantly laid to lawn and features mature hedging, block boundary walls, a cobblelock pathway and a mostly enclosed pergola. A rear gate provides access to a large communal green area.\n\nNo. 30 Elm Park offers an excellent opportunity to acquire a stylish and versatile family home in a well-established and popular residential location. With its modernised and extended accommodation, generous gardens, garage and convenient location, viewing is strongly recommended to fully appreciate all this property has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nTimber flooring, door to kitchen/dining/living room, door to ground floor bedroom and stairs to first floor.\n\nKitchen Dining Living Room - \nLarge openplan space with traditional style kitchen, dining space and the ling area features a solid fuel stove. Double doors off the living area grant access to the rear garden. A door off the kitchen leads to the utility room and ground floor bathroom.\n\nUtility Room - \nTile flooring, plumbed for washing machine, dryer, countertop space with sink & shelving. Rear access door and door to bathroom.\n\nBathroom - \nTile flooring, half tiled walls, WC, WHB, fully tiled shower area with pump shower and rear aspect stained glass window.\n\nBedroom 1 (Ground Floor) - \nLaminate timber flooring, solid fuel fireplace with cast iron insert and timber surround & large front aspect window.\n\nLanding - \nTimber flooring, doors to three bedrooms, main bathroom & hot-press.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nDouble bedroom, laminate timber flooring and rear aspect window.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nDouble bedroom, laminate timber flooring and front aspect window.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nSingle bedroom, built in storage over the stairs and front aspect window.\n\nBathroom - \nFully tiled throughout, WC, WHB with vanity unit, bath unit with curved shower screen and electric shower. Rear aspect frosted window.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Stylish three/four-bedroom family home</li><li>Modernised and extended by the current Vendors</li><li>Spacious open-plan kitchen/living/dining room</li><li>Ground-floor bedroom with open fireplace</li><li>Enclosed garage and excellent off-street parking</li><li>Generous gardens with pergola and access to communal green area</li><li>Oil fired central heating</li><li>Mains Sewerage & water</li><li>Fibre broadband</ul>"
      },
